-- ind-c-tests-powers.l4: independent tests (ind-c) of who may or must act under Chapter 6, through the encoding's
-- regulative rules.  A power or duty whose precondition fails is FULFILLED (nothing arises); one whose precondition
-- holds is a live PARTY ... MAY/MUST/SHANT.  A live rule cannot be compared with EQUALS (the binary says "Trying to
-- check equality on types that do not support it"), so the live cases are printed by #EVAL for a reader to check
-- and only the FULFILLED cases are asserted.  Scenario ids of work/ind-c/expectations.md.

§ `ind-c: powers and duties of Chapter 6`

§§ `Fixtures`

`ind-c individual` MEANS Person WITH `reference for the person` IS "ind-1", `kind of person` IS `an individual`

GIVEN what IS A `Listed violation`
GIVETH A Violation
`ind-c a violation of` what MEANS
    Violation WITH `the violator` IS `ind-c individual`
                 , `the listed violation` IS what
                 , `reference for the act` IS "act-1"
                 , `date of the act` IS YMD 2027 3 10

§§ `s 41: the Commissioner may impose; the Minister may change the Schedule`

-- s.41(a): Chapter 6 in force and the Commissioner authorised: the power is live.
#EVAL `s 41(a) — the Commissioner may impose the financial sanction for` (`ind-c a violation of` `work with no licence at all`) TRUE TRUE
-- G5: Chapter 6 not in force: no power arises.
#ASSERT `s 41(a) — the Commissioner may impose the financial sanction for` (`ind-c a violation of` `work with no licence at all`) FALSE TRUE EQUALS FULFILLED
-- B1/B6/B7 (s.41(b)): both approvals and within the cap: live; no consent of the Minister of Justice, or no committee: none.
#EVAL `s 41(b) — the Minister may change the Third Schedule by order` `the Third Schedule` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `s 41(b) — the Minister may change the Third Schedule by order` `the Third Schedule` FALSE TRUE EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT `s 41(b) — the Minister may change the Third Schedule by order` `the Third Schedule` TRUE FALSE EQUALS FULFILLED

§§ `s 42(a): the duty to give notice of intention`

#EVAL `s 42(a) — the Commissioner must give notice of intention` TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- No intention to impose: no duty.
#ASSERT `s 42(a) — the Commissioner must give notice of intention` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS FULFILLED
-- Chapter 6 not in force: no duty.
#ASSERT `s 42(a) — the Commissioner must give notice of intention` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FULFILLED

§§ `s 46(b) and s 47(c)`

-- C18: the Minister's power to set lower amounts needs the Minister of Justice's consent AND the committee's approval.
#EVAL `s 46(b) — the Minister may set the circumstances and rates for lower amounts` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `s 46(b) — the Minister may set the circumstances and rates for lower amounts` FALSE TRUE EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT `s 46(b) — the Minister may set the circumstances and rates for lower amounts` TRUE FALSE EQUALS FULFILLED
-- s.47(c): the Commissioner SHALL publish the updated amounts in Reshumot: a live duty.
#EVAL `s 47(c) — the Commissioner must publish the updated amounts in Reshumot`

§§ `s 50(a), s 52(a), s 54, s 55, s 57`

-- D13/D15: instalments: a live power on a request for 12; none without a request; none for 13.
#EVAL `s 50(a) — the Commissioner may allow payment by instalments` TRUE 12 TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `s 50(a) — the Commissioner may allow payment by instalments` FALSE 12 TRUE TRUE EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT `s 50(a) — the Commissioner may allow payment by instalments` TRUE 13 TRUE TRUE EQUALS FULFILLED
-- D17/D18: the warning power: live with AG-approved procedures; none without.
#EVAL `s 52(a) — the Commissioner may give the violator an administrative warning` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `s 52(a) — the Commissioner may give the violator an administrative warning` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FULFILLED
-- D23/D24: after a warning, a continuing or repeat breach: the Commissioner SHALL give a notice of intention.
#EVAL `s 54 — the Commissioner must give notice of intention after a warning` TRUE
#ASSERT `s 54 — the Commissioner must give notice of intention after a warning` FALSE EQUALS FULFILLED
-- E1: a sanction already imposed for the act: the Commissioner SHAN'T impose another (a live prohibition).
#EVAL `s 55 — the Commissioner shall not impose a further sanction for the same act` TRUE
#ASSERT `s 55 — the Commissioner shall not impose a further sanction for the same act` FALSE EQUALS FULFILLED
-- F1: a sanction imposed: the Commissioner SHALL publish; none imposed: nothing to publish.
#EVAL `s 57(a) — the Commissioner must publish the particulars of the financial sanction` TRUE FALSE `an individual`
#ASSERT `s 57(a) — the Commissioner must publish the particulars of the financial sanction` FALSE FALSE `an individual` EQUALS FULFILLED
-- F5: an appeal filed: the Commissioner SHALL publish it and its result.
#EVAL `s 57(b) — the Commissioner must publish the appeal and its result` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `s 57(b) — the Commissioner must publish the appeal and its result` FALSE FALSE EQUALS FULFILLED
-- F6: when the publication period ends, the Ministry SHALL apply measures against viewing, if accepted means exist.
#EVAL `s 57(e) — the Ministry must apply technological measures when the publication that began on` (YMD 2027 5 10) `for` `an individual` `ends, if accepted means exist:` TRUE
#ASSERT `s 57(e) — the Ministry must apply technological measures when the publication that began on` (YMD 2027 5 10) `for` `an individual` `ends, if accepted means exist:` FALSE EQUALS FULFILLED
